{
 "schema": 1,
 "data": "rola_devtools.cells.carry:carry_cell",
 "note": "THE CARRY CELLS: a routed recurrence's input as data. One record per cell; every package's tests and measurements read these. A record declares a draw, a shape and the state it binds, never how a kernel runs it: a launch shape, a window grid or an arm key is the arm's.",
 "fields": {
  "name": "the cell's identity",
  "seed": "the random seed the draw is taken from (written in 2026-09-15 as crc32(name) & 0xFFFF, the seed each name implied, so no draw moved)",
  "widths": "the per-level digit counts B_l of the routing (powers of two at or above 16)",
  "dv": "the value width DV",
  "tokens": "L, the sequence length in tokens",
  "draw": "dense | alt | both | cohort | dead | deposit | tied | anti | cold | readonly | concentrated | onehot | flip -- which support structure the routing is drawn with (rola_devtools.cells.carry.realize and _corner); `dead` puts zero amplitude everywhere and `deposit` makes exactly one token write exactly one leaf",
  "k_tok": "nonzeros per row per sparse level; a property of the DRAW and never told to a kernel",
  "cohort": "for draw=cohort, the run of consecutive tokens sharing one contiguous digit window",
  "support": "the leading fraction of each level's digits the draw may use (structured truncation); for draw=cold, the fraction of level zero's digits the WRITE side may use",
  "backing": "dense | paged -- the state backing the cell binds: one contiguous plane, or pages mapped from a shared arena",
  "state": "none | fresh | carried -- whether the cell binds an entry state and chains; a carried cell's entry state is drawn with it (RealizedCell.entry)",
  "tier": "oracle | probe | both -- who the cell is sized for: an fp64 reference, a measurement, or both. The `one-box-*` cells are sized so N is one CTA box: a sanitizer sees the whole shared memory at 1/256 a flagship cell's record memory",
  "regime": "where the draw sits on every axis of rola_devtools.cells.regimes.REGIME_AXES; realize proves it and refuses a draw that is elsewhere. null for dead and deposit, which state their support themselves"
 },
